  button_label: Book an Appointment
causes:
  title: Causes of Neurological Disorders
  intro: Neurological disorders can develop due to a variety of factors that affect the brain, spinal cord, or nervous system. Some causes are inherited, while others result from injuries, infections, or lifestyle-related conditions. Understanding these causes can help with early prevention, diagnosis, and effective treatment.
  items:
    - title: Genetic Factors
      text: Some neurological disorders are passed down through family genes, increasing the risk of developing certain conditions. These inherited genetic changes can affect how the brain and nervous system function over time. Although genetic disorders cannot always be prevented, early screening and medical care can help manage symptoms and improve quality of life.
    - title: Brain Injury & Trauma
      text: Traumatic injuries to the head or spinal cord can damage nerve cells and disrupt communication within the nervous system. Falls, road accidents, sports injuries, or severe blows to the head are common causes. Depending on the severity of the injury, individuals may experience long-term neurological symptoms that require ongoing treatment and rehabilitation.
    - title: Infections & Medical Conditions
      text: Certain infections, autoimmune diseases, strokes, and chronic medical conditions can harm the brain and nervous system. Inflammation or reduced blood flow may interfere with normal nerve function, leading to neurological complications. Prompt diagnosis and appropriate treatment can reduce the risk of permanent damage and support better recovery.
conditions:
