      Our nutrition approach for dementia focuses on maintaining adequate nutrition, hydration, and healthy body weight as eating patterns and appetite may change over time. We develop practical meal plans based on the patient’s preferences, abilities, medical needs, and stage of disease.

      We encourage nutrient-dense, easy-to-eat meals and simple routines that can make eating more manageable. Our goal is to support nutritional status, energy, and quality of life for patients and their caregivers.
    image: dementia.jpeg
  - title: "Parkinson’s Disease"
    text: |-
      Our nutrition care for Parkinson’s Disease focuses on maintaining strength, energy, healthy weight, and adequate nutrient intake. Plans are personalized according to symptoms, appetite, activity level, swallowing concerns, and individual dietary needs.

      We provide guidance on balanced meals, protein, fiber, hydration, and practical eating strategies. Where medication timing may affect nutrition, dietary recommendations can be coordinated with the patient’s healthcare plan.
    image: ension.jpg
  - title: Neuropathy (Especially Diabetic)
    text: |-
      Our nutrition approach for diabetic neuropathy focuses on supporting blood glucose management and overall metabolic health. Personalized nutrition plans are designed around the patient’s dietary habits, diabetes management, lifestyle, and nutritional requirements.

      We emphasize balanced meals, appropriate carbohydrate portions, fiber-rich foods, quality protein, and essential nutrients. The goal is to support better metabolic health while promoting healthy eating habits and overall well-being.
    image: nueropathy.jpg
